Your metamodel is shaping up very well, and this structure captures the essence of MySQL schemas quite nicely. Defining EnumType as a class with AllowedValues and linking EnumField to exactly one EnumType aligns perfectly with database enum semantics.

To maintain data integrity, enforcing uniqueness for labels, identifiers, and names within their respective scopes is crucial, as well as ensuring each DataGrouping belongs to exactly one DataStore, each DataField to exactly one DataGrouping, and EnumFields always reference an EnumType.

I’ll create constraints for you using OCL-like expressions (adapted for Jjodel) to guarantee these unique textual identifiers and required references.

Here’s how you can add these constraints:

```jjscript
# Constraints for MySQL Database Schema Metamodel

# Each DataStore label must be unique across all DataStores
constraint uniqueDataStoreLabels in DataStore {
  DataStore.allInstances()->isUnique(label)
}

# Each DataGrouping identifier must be unique within its containing DataStore
constraint uniqueDataGroupingIdentifiers in DataGrouping {
  DataStore.allInstances()->exists(ds | ds.dataGroupings->includes(self)) and
  DataStore.allInstances()->forAll(ds |
    ds.dataGroupings->select(dg | dg.identifier = self.identifier)->size() = 1
  )
}

# Each DataField name must be unique within its containing DataGrouping
constraint uniqueDataFieldNames in DataGrouping {
  dataFields->isUnique(name)
}

# Each EnumType literal values must be unique within EnumType
constraint uniqueAllowedValueValues in EnumType {
  allowedValues->isUnique(value)
}

# Each EnumField must reference exactly one EnumType
constraint enumFieldHasEnumType in EnumField {
  enumType <> null
}
```

These constraints maintain uniqueness at the proper containment levels, preventing naming clashes and ensuring all enum fields are properly typed.

You can add these constraints via the Jjodel Properties panel on each metaclass or use Jjodel's constraint editor to insert them. Jjodel supports OCL-like syntax validation to enforce these rules at model editing time.

